{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"rg -n -B1 -A7 'sr_refs = \\\\[\\\"SR-165\\\"\\\\]|verifies = \\\\[\\\"SR-165\\\"' docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml docs/test/test-cases.toml; git diff --name-only aa36a5b6...452eec0 -- docs/status.md docs/process.toml; git status --porcelain\"","aggregated_output":"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1762-[design.LLR-172]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:1763:sr_refs = [\"SR-165\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1764-title = \"Component derivation record: element completeness + the ranking recompute\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1765-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/trajectory_arch.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1766-code_symbol = \"component_findings\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1767-detail = \"\"\"Extends the existing component pass — the one home that already reads docs/requirements/components.toml and already emits CMP findings — with the derivation-record rules SR-165 states, rather than adding a second reader of the same registry. Per live CMP row: the record must declare the candidate partitions considered, the objective and the constraints they were scored against, a score per candidate, the selected partition, and the human ruling that named the components and adopted it; a missing element is one finding naming the row AND the element. Two derived rules on top of presence, because presence alone is satisfiable by a record that says nothing: (1) THE RANKING RECOMPUTES — re-rank the recorded candidates from the record's own objective, constraints and scores and compare with the recorded order, a mismatch being a finding, which is what makes the record falsifiable without a reviewer re-running a model session; (2) A SELECTION THE SCORES DO NOT RANK FIRST is a finding unless the record carries a human override naming that choice, so a legitimate \"the scores said A, the human chose B\" is expressible and an unexplained one is not. Vacuous by construction on a project declaring no components, and on the example -000 rows. NOT BUILT YET: the record cells do not exist on the CMP schema today — recorded as open debt on this row and TC-166; SR-165 carries Test verification precisely because the check is mechanizable, and this is the debt that verification incurs, recorded rather than silently owed.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1768-rationale = \"\"\"The check belongs where component_findings already is for the reason the census keeps applying: a second module reading components.toml would be a second answer to \"is this partition recorded\", and the two would drift. The recompute is the load-bearing half — an element-presence check passes on a record whose scores contradict its own conclusion, which is the exact failure SN-040 exists to catch (the next reviser cannot tell load-bearing boundaries from accidents). The override arm is what stops the recompute rule from forbidding human judgement: the requirement is that a departure from the scores is RECORDED, never that it is disallowed.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1769-test_refs = \"TC-166\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1770-status = \"Approved\"\n--\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1667-[test.TC-166]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml:1668:verifies = [\"SR-165\", \"LLR-172\"]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1669-level = \"Integration\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1670-method = \"\"\"Run trace.py's component pass over fixture component registries: (a) a complete derivation record passes silently; (b) a record omitting each element in turn — candidate partitions, objective, constraints, any candidate's score, the selected partition, the human ruling — is reported once per omission, naming the row and the missing element; (c) a record whose recorded ranking does not recompute from its own objective, constraints and scores is reported; (d) a selected partition the recorded scores do not rank first is reported, and the SAME record with a recorded human override naming that choice is silent; (e) a project declaring no components, and the shipped example -000 rows, are vacuous.\"\"\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1671-tier = \"Full\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1672-expected = \"Satisfies SR-165 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-172 detail contract\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1673-automated = \"Yes\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1674-evidence = \"tests/test_components_registry.py (to be extended at implementation)\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1675-status = \"Approved\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nReviewed: 452eec010d33a712de5f7beba5330968d8cc6a89\n\nVerified: Independent convergence review of the prescribed full-lane diff, WI-976's complete spec, its item-14 specref and quoted owner ruling, PROCESS sections 3/5/6, the kit-change rubric, and the cited registry rows and their existing counterparts. Hunted silent omitted/extra hat questions first, fail-open composition second, and retirement/data-loss regressions third. The specified test selection passed (452 passed, 2 skipped); trajectory and strict integrity checks passed. Actual compose and mkprompt flows preserve separate parent contexts, include amended SRs' parents in mixed rounds, reject malformed rosters where the optional slot is used, and keep outcome lines outside the ruling grammar. No new reachable defect was found. The worktree remains clean. This verdict does not attest the owner-held act or the subsequent TC-211 execution.\n\nCommands:\n- \"'`git rev-parse HEAD` -> `452eec010d33a712de5f7beba5330968d8cc6a89` before running checks.\n- `Get-Content CLAUDE.md`, `.agents/skills/antidote/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/coordinator-cycle/SKILL.md`, WI-976'\"'s spec, and \"'`docs/rubrics/kit-change-review.md`; targeted `Get-Content`/`Select-Object` reads of PROCESS, item 14, the changed scripts/tests, and the authored implementation plan -> governing rules and changed behavior inspected. No earlier verdict file, decisions file, filed critique, lane commit subject, or implementer session note was opened.\n- `git diff aa36a5b6e2bc47fe9960bbc4a0727c04c9571f36...452eec010d33a712de5f7beba5330968d8cc6a89 -- . '\"':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/decisions' ':(exclude)docs/plans/*/critique-*' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'\"'` (stat and path-grouped patches) -> 42 changed files; code, tests, requirements, instructions, shipping notice and generated changes inspected.\n- Targeted `rg -n` searches in the existing SN/SR/LLR/TC/IF registries for the changed IDs, perspective obligations and retained counterparts -> no conflicting obligation, new overlapping capability, or changed limit found. `rg` retirement sweep across the declared live surfaces, excluding RESYNC'\"'s retirement notices -> no remaining sidecar path, record command, retired row citation or command-only symbol; the loose \"'`hats record` pattern also matched unrelated English in trace'\"'s docstring.\n- \"'`git show f6c7360f:docs/log.d/2026-09-06-sn036-owner-ruling.md` -> independently read the quoted ruling, its four acts and prohibition on the sidecar/check.\n- `git log -p --format=%h aa36a5b6e2bc47fe9960bbc4a0727c04c9571f36..452eec010d33a712de5f7beba5330968d8cc6a89 -- project-trajectory/scripts/plan_briefs.py project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py scripts/coordinator/mkprompt.py tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py tests/test_prompts.py`; `git log --format=%h` over the changed implementation paths -> pre-fix implementations located without commit messages.\n- With `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-25b-leg20` and `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`: `C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n 2 --basetemp C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-25b-leg20/g1a/wi-976 tests/test_plan_briefs.py tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py tests/test_prompts.py tests/test_hats.py tests/test_dogfood_sync.py tests/test_spine_carrier.py tests/test_trace.py tests/test_trace_hats.py` -> `452 passed, 2 skipped in 397.59s (0:06:37)`.\n- `C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe project-trajectory/scripts/check_trajectory.py --strict` -> `check_trajectory: clean (973 work item(s), 863 done (89%), 34 cancelled, graph acyclic).` Exit 0; advisory warnings are not reprod